# Looks done, not wired

`wiring-verification.mdc` catches unmounted routes and Coming Soon tabs. This rule catches a **complete-looking** feature whose live UI, seed IDs, or e2e still assume the old model.

## Must verify

1. Trace the **user** write path, not only Format Editor. If scoring/standings **read** `pod_membership`, lock-in (or the seeded first-round path) must persist it — a Generate-only write is a ship blocker.
2. API types + client method + a **visible control that calls it** + Playwright that clicks that path. Empty membership must not invent a fake “Pod 1.”
3. Seed + Playwright must follow the **new** paradigm in the same change. Leaving `match-play-methods` / full-sim `completePlayableSeries` on a pinfall pods feature is “looks done.”
4. Forbidden: fallbacks that invent valid-looking data when the real payload is missing.
5. Grep callers from the live entrypoint (`ScoringSurfaceRouter`, seed event IDs, Playwright copy). Do not trust “Pod Match Board” leftovers or markdown ratings.

## Flavor (this repo)

`ScoringSurfaceRouter` (pinfall pods vs H2H), e2e seed IDs, Playwright hitting the new copy (`Generate pods`, rollover checkboxes), and `PUT /side-actions/roster-signups` from `RosterRolloverControl`.

At commit/cleanup/push time also follow `cleanup-false-wiring-duplication.mdc`.
